/// A value that may move to another thread, or be lent to one as `&mut` (spec §22.2).
///
/// Nothing implements it: a type is `Send` when every field is, worked out by the compiler as
/// it works out whether a type is plain. Numbers, `bool`, plain structs and arrays of them
/// are; a raw pointer that is not `own` is not, since what it points at may be anyone's, and
/// so neither is anything holding one, `Rc` and `Weak` included. Only `std` makes an
/// exception, for a container whose memory the compiler places for the thread (§22.6).
///
/// ```dz
/// fn start<T: Send>(value: T) -> Thread { … }
/// ```
pub trait Send {
}
